[0m[0m
[1mKey implementation decisions:[22m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
1. [1mGF(2) polynomial arithmetic[22m: The core [38;5;10m_mm_clmulepi64_si128[0m intrinsic (carry-less multiply) is implemented as [38;5;10mclmul64[0m using bit-by-bit XOR over 64 iterations. All 128-bit values use Rust's native [38;5;10mu128[0m type instead of [38;5;10m__m128i[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
2. [1mSSE intrinsic translations[22m: All SSE operations ([38;5;10m_mm_load_si128[0m, [38;5;10m_mm_slli_epi64[0m, [38;5;10m_mm_srli_si128[0m, [38;5;10m_mm_shuffle_epi8[0m, etc.) are translated to equivalent [38;5;10mu128[0m arithmetic with helper functions like [38;5;10mfrom_halves[0m, [38;5;10mlo64[0m, [38;5;10mhi64[0m, [38;5;10mleftshift1[0m, [38;5;10mleftshift2[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
3. [1mSmall key handling[22m: When the random data is smaller than [38;5;10mRANDOM_BYTES_NEEDED_FOR_CLHASH[0m (1064 bytes), the function interprets the first two [38;5;10mu64[0m values as seeds and generates the full key via [38;5;10mget_random_key_for_clhash[0m. This handles the test cases that pass only 16 bytes of random data.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
4. [1mKey generation[22m: The [38;5;10mxorshift128plus[0m PRNG matches the C implementation exactly, producing identical keys for the same seeds.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
